horitative and helps nothing, because in most cases the number was never earned. Learning to spot a fabricated rating tells you which directories to trust.</p></div>\n<nav class=\"toc\" aria-label=\"Table of contents\"><p class=\"toc-h\">Contents</p><ul><li><a href=\"#the-tell-everything-scores-the-same-1\">The tell: everything scores the same</a></li><li><a href=\"#the-other-tell-the-score-tracks-the-position-2\">The other tell: the score tracks the position</a></li><li><a href=\"#what-honest-looks-like-3\">What honest looks like</a></li><li><a href=\"#why-dark-ero-shows-a-date-not-just-a-score-4\">Why Dark-Ero shows a date, not just a score</a></li><li><a href=\"#more-guides-guides-5\">More Guides guides</a></li></ul></nav>\n<div class=\"article-meta\"><span>Dark-Ero editorial</span><span>2026-09-30</span></div>\n<article class=\"prose\">\n    <p style=\"font-size:18px;color:var(--text)\">Most directories score every site 9-point-something. Here is how to tell a real assessment from a formula.</p>\n    <p>Adult directories love a rating. A big number next to every site looks authoritative and helps nothing, because in most cases the number was never earned. Learning to spot a fabricated rating tells you which directories to trust.</p><h2 id=\"the-tell-everything-scores-the-same-1\">The tell: everything scores the same</h2><p>When every site on a list sits between 9.0 and 9.9, the score isn't measuring quality — it's decoration. Real assessments produce spread. Some sites are mediocre; a rating system that never says so isn't rating anything.</p><h2 id=\"the-other-tell-the-score-tracks-the-position-2\">The other tell: the score tracks the position</h2><p>If the top listing scores 9.9 and each one below drops by a tenth, the 'rating' is just the rank wearing a costume. This is a genuinely common trick, and once you see it you can't unsee it.</p><div class=\"callout\"><p>A rating is only meaningful if the directory tells you when the site was checked and by whom. A number with no date behind it is a decoration, not an assessment.</p></div><h2 id=\"what-honest-looks-like-3\">What honest looks like</h2><p>An honest directory does two things: it shows the date a site was actually reviewed, and it admits when a site hasn't been reviewed yet rather than inventing a number to fill the gap. That is less impressive-looking and far more useful.</p><h2 id=\"why-dark-ero-shows-a-date-not-just-a-score-4\">Why Dark-Ero shows a date, not just a score</h2><p>We display a review date on every assessed site, and we mark the ones we haven't reached yet as exactly that. It means our numbers cover fewer sites — and it means the numbers we do show were earned by someone opening the site and looking.</p>\n    <div class=\"callout safe\"><p>Browsing this topic? See the <a href=\"/category/premium/\">Premium</a> section of the directory for hand-checked sites.</p></div>\n    <hr class=\"divider\" style=\"margin:34px 0\">\n    <p style=\"font-size:14px;color:var(--muted)\">This guide is general information, not legal or security advice. Laws on adult content vary by country — check what applies where you live.</p>\n  </article>\n  <div style=\"display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:30px 0\"><a class=\"btn btn-ghost\" href=\"/blog/ai-adult-tools-and-your-data-check-this-before-you-upload/\">← AI adult tools and your data: chec…</a><a class=\"btn btn-ghost\" href=\"/blog/vr-adult-content-headset-compatibility-explained-plainly/\">VR adult content: headset compatib… →</a></div>\n  <section class=\"section\" style=\"padding-top:0\">\n    <div class=\"section-head\"><h2 id=\"more-guides-guides-5\">More Guides guides</h2><a href=\"/blog/topic/guides/\">All →</a></div>\n    <div class=\"post-list\"><article class=\"post-card\">\n      <div class=\"tagline\"><a href=\"/blog/topic/guides/\" style=\"color:inherit\">Guides</a></div>\n      <h3><a href=\"/blog/free-versus-premium-what-you-are-actually-paying-for/\">Free versus premium: what you are actually paying for</a></h3>\n      <p>The real trade is not price against no-price. It is your attention against your money.</p>\n      <a class=\"more\" href=\"/blog/free-versus-premium-what-you-are-actually-paying-for/\">Read guide →</a>\n    </article><article class=\"post-card\">\n      <div class=\"tagline\"><a href=\"/blog/topic/guides/\" style=\"color:inherit\">Guides</a></div>\n      <h3><a href=\"/blog/reading-cam-site-pricing-before-it-reads-your-wallet/\">Reading cam site pricing before it reads your wallet</a></h3>\n      <p>Tokens, tips and private shows are designed to obscure the real cost. Here is how to see through it.</p>\n      <a class=\"more\" href=\"/blog/reading-cam-site-pricing-before-it-reads-your-wallet/\">Read guide →</a>\n    </article><article class=\"post-card\">\n      <div class=\"tagline\"><a href=\"/blog/topic/safety/\" style=\"color:inherit\">Safety</a></div>\n      <h3><a href=\"/blog/how-to-tell-a-real-adult-site-from-a-malware-trap/\">How to tell a real adult site from a malware trap</a></h3>\n      <p>The five signals that separate a legitimate platform from a page that just wants your browser.</p>\n      <a class=\"more\" href=\"/blog/how-to-tell-a-real-adult-site-from-a-malware-trap/\">Read guide →</a>\n    </article></div>\n  </section>\n</article></main>\n<footer class=\"site-foot de-foot\">\n  <div class=\"de-foot-band\"><div class=\"container\">\n    <div class=\"de-foot-top\">\n      <a class=\"brand\" href=\"/\"><img class=\"brand-logo\" src=\"/assets/logo.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"42\" height=\"42\"><span class=\"wordmark\"><b>Dark</b><span class=\"ero\">-Ero</span></span></a>\n      <p>An independent adult-site directory. Listings go straight to the site. Scores appear only after a real review.</p>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"de-foot-icons\">\n      <a href=\"/contact/\" aria-label=\"Contact\"><svg width=\"18\" height=\"18\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"5\" wid